exity",["Dynamic Programming Reference","Related References"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-0","Enum",[]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-9","Also known as: enumeration, enumerated type",["Enum"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-56","A distinct data type that consists of a set of named constants, representing a collection of related values",["Enum"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-167","Each named constant is called a variant (in some languages) or enumerator",["Enum"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-248","Key Benefits",["Enum"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-267","Improved Readability and Maintainability",["Enum","Key Benefits"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-316","Using descriptive names instead of arbitrary numbers or strings makes code more self-explanatory",["Enum","Key Benefits","Improved Readability and Maintainability"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-418","Example: Color.RED is clearer than using 0 to represent a color",["Enum","Key Benefits","Improved Readability and Maintainability"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-491","Type Safety",["Enum","Key Benefits"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-511","Restricts variables to predefined values, reducing the risk of invalid assignments",["Enum","Key Benefits","Type Safety"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-599","Ensures only valid, expected values are used, preventing bugs",["Enum","Key Benefits","Type Safety"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-666","Encapsulation",["Enum","Key Benefits"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-688","Groups related constants within a single data type",["Enum","Key Benefits","Encapsulation"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-744","Organizes code more effectively and reduces errors from using unrelated constants",["Enum","Key Benefits","Encapsulation"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-831","Common Use Cases",["Enum"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-854","State Management: Representing discrete states (e.g., PENDING, IN_PROGRESS, COMPLETED)",["Enum","Common Use Cases"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-955","Configuration Options: Defining sets of options or modes (e.g., logging levels: DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR)",["Enum","Common Use Cases"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-1080","Control Flow: Using enums in switch or case statements to handle different scenarios",["Enum","Common Use Cases"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-1177","Error Handling: Representing success/failure states (e.g., Result<T, E> in Rust)",["Enum","Common Use Cases"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-1268","Nullable Values: Representing optional values (e.g., Option<T> in Rust, Optional<T> in Java)",["Enum","Common Use Cases"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-1373","Language Implementations",["Enum"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-1404","C",["Enum","Language Implementations"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-1414","Declared using the enum keyword",["Enum","Language Implementations","C"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-1453","Creates a set of named integer constants",["Enum","Language Implementations","C"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-1499","By default, values start at 0 and increment",["Enum","Language Implementations","C"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-1642","C++",["Enum","Language Implementations"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-1654","Supports unscoped enums (similar to C)",["Enum","Language Implementations","C++"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-1698","C++11 introduced scoped enums with enum class for better type safety",["Enum","Language Implementations","C++"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-1774","Prevents implicit conversions",["Enum","Language Implementations","C++"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-1901","Java",["Enum","Language Implementations"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-1914","More robust enums that can have methods and fields",["Enum","Language Implementations","Java"]],["Programming/Enum/","source-block-1970","Can implement interfaces",["Enum"